From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:33:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: core: Fix supplied_from for nodes with several
 supplies

power_supply_check_supplies() allocates supplied_from with room for a
single pointer, whatever the number of power-supplies references, and
then stores a separately allocated array of cnt - 1 chars in that one
slot. __power_supply_populate_supplied_from() then fills in one slot per
reference index, but bumps num_supplies once for every registered supply
whose node matches.

A device that registers two power supplies on one node, such as bq256xx
with its charger and battery supplies, therefore leaves num_supplies at
2 with a single slot, and __power_supply_is_supplied_by() reads past the
array and passes whatever it finds there to strcmp(). On the Zinwa Q25,
a battery with power-supplies pointing at its bq25601 charger crashed
this way with a NULL pointer dereference as soon as the charger came
online.

Allocate one slot per reference and take the first supply registered for
each reference, so that num_supplies never exceeds the slots filled.

Signed-off-by: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/power_supply_core.c | 13 ++++---------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_core.c b/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_core.c
index a446d3d0..ce001805 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_core.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_core.c
@@ -203,7 +203,7 @@ static int __power_supply_populate_supplied_from(struct power_supply *epsy,
 		if (IS_ERR(np))
 			break;
 
-		if (np == epsy->dev.fwnode) {
+		if (np == epsy->dev.fwnode && !psy->supplied_from[i - 1]) {
 			dev_dbg(&psy->dev, "%s: Found supply : %s\n",
 				psy->desc->name, epsy->desc->name);
 			psy->supplied_from[i-1] = (char *)epsy->desc->name;
@@ -292,18 +292,13 @@ static int power_supply_check_supplies(struct power_supply *psy)
 	if (cnt == 1)
 		return 0;
 
-	/* All supplies found, allocate char ** array for filling */
-	psy->supplied_from = devm_kzalloc(&psy->dev, sizeof(*psy->supplied_from),
+	/* All supplies found, allocate one name per reference for filling */
+	psy->supplied_from = devm_kcalloc(&psy->dev, cnt - 1,
+					  sizeof(*psy->supplied_from),
 					  GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!psy->supplied_from)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
-	*psy->supplied_from = devm_kcalloc(&psy->dev,
-					   cnt - 1, sizeof(**psy->supplied_from),
-					   GFP_KERNEL);
-	if (!*psy->supplied_from)
-		return -ENOMEM;
-
 	return power_supply_populate_supplied_from(psy);
 }
 #else
